---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

---

<Layout title="About - Jeni Hoyt" description="About Jeni.">
  <Header />
  
  <main id="main-content">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About Me</h1>
      <p class="intro">
       I'm a front-end developer who specializes in web accessibility and loves translating designs into clean, semantic web experiences. I consider myself a lifelong learner and make an effort to stay current with changes in core front-end technologies. 
I decided to specialize in web accessibility when I realized how much of the web is still inaccessible to so many people. And since I love to find problems and fix them, testing and remediating accessibility issues comes naturally to me.
I'm a DHS Certified Trusted Tester for Web, I'm currently pursuing my CPACC certification, and I regularly perform automated and manual accessibility testing.
I'm looking for a role where accessibility is the focus — whether that's testing, remediation, conformance analysis, or some combination. I think my background as a developer makes me a stronger accessibility professional: I don't just find the issues, I understand where they come from and how to fix them.
</p>
    
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .container {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--spacing);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

</style>